d3d11: give a shared surface's creator a moment before handing it to somebody
 who would find it empty

What 0018 leaves: one start in sixteen still comes up with Word's navigation
rail at two colours, its title bar at one, and the full black band -- all three
together, which is what says they are one fault.  The shape of it is in 0018's
own evidence: the participant that did not create the surface can acquire it,
on key 0, before its creator has released anything into it at all.  On Windows
that participant sees the creator's live pixels, because the storage really is
shared and nothing has to be carried.  Here there is nothing to give it, so it
composites a whole frame from a texture that has never held anything, and
Office does not draw that content again.

This waits for the creator, and the two things that make it safe are the two
things it does not do:

  - **It does not take the surface while it waits.**  The creator can acquire
    it and get on with drawing, which is the whole point.
  - **It never extends the caller's own timeout,** and it gives up after 250 ms
    regardless.  The creator may itself be blocked on a key only this
    participant can release, and waiting for content in that position is a
    deadlock; giving up and taking the empty surface is exactly what happens
    today.  So the worst case this can produce is a late frame, and a caller
    that passed timeout 0 is unaffected -- for those the wait is zero-length by
    construction.

Two WARNs come with it, because both states they report are anomalies worth
seeing: `altars-content-wait` when the wait engages and again if it succeeds,
and `altars-empty-acquire` when it expires and a participant takes an unwritten
surface anyway -- the case that loses a frame.  In an ordinary start-up none of
them fires, and that is the point: the wait is inert until the ordering
inverts.  What is *not* yet measured is the thing it exists for -- catching the
inversion takes a run in which it happens, and at one start in sixteen that is
a long wait.  So this is a change argued from a mechanism 0018's evidence
names, with an instrument attached that will say plainly whether it ever
engages and whether it helps when it does.  Read the WARNs before believing it
works.

--- a/dlls/d3d11/shared.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/shared.c
